{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head e18b6c71655fa477594a507129eb69bafbda8390, tree df7baac8dde3283a767b0a9717b0acbc8eb8c8c2, on builder/cb1-ls1-source-20261115, all 25 artifacts, for request cfbf11ba under my promise 939fa198 and standing da772676. This verdict names all three implementations: CB-1 (request b5f200f2, promise 9b083032, report 81194b0f, the CB-1 note, primary), LS-1 (request 3bacbc5e, promise 630a37a0, report b5cc7eee, the LS-1 note) and LC-3 (request 7b51d924, promise fa55582b, report fde92990, `apps/room/wrangler.lending.jsonc`). `gs review --prepare` resolved all three bindings and reports at this head, with each request closing on the sealed receipt. I read the head from the shared object store. The branch is not on origin.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `apps/room/celld/mac/application-settings.mjs`, new. A project carries both `r2_buckets` and `APPLICATION_TRUST`, or neither. The bucket list must be exactly one row with the two keys `binding` and `bucket_name`, set to `APPLICATION_CONTENT` and `application-content`. The trust text is at most 64 KiB and must pass `readApplicationTrust` from `packages/client/src/application-trust.ts`, the production parser, so no second trust grammar exists. `readApplicationProject` reads a staged `wrangler.json` with `parseStrict`, so a duplicate key cannot hide a second value. `stageApplicationSettings` accepts only an absolute, canonical, non-symlink regular file of at most 64 KiB, checks its text before any output exists, and copies the text byte for byte into `vars`. The `--check-trust` entry reads stdin as fatal UTF-8 up to the same limit and prints only \"Invalid application settings\".\n- `apps/room/celld/mac/prepare-project.mjs`. The new `applications` stage runs before the `output` stage, so a bad trust file creates no private directory. The arguments parser takes each of four flags at most once, in pairs, and requires the three old ones. The written project text must still fit in 64 KiB.\n- `apps/room/celld/mac/prepare-github.mjs`. It reads the original project through `readApplicationProject` and `applicationProjectSettings`, removes `r2_buckets` before the maintained-settings comparison, and adds `APPLICATION_TRUST` to the optional variables.\n- `apps/room/celld/mac/deploy.py`. `prepared_project` excludes `r2_buckets` from the closed comparison only when the pair is present, requires the exact one-row list, and admits `APPLICATION_TRUST` as the one added variable. Every existing closed check runs first. Only then does `check_application_trust` start `node application-settings.mjs --check-trust` with the trust text on stdin, a 10-second timeout and no output. Any failure refuses with a fixed message.\n- `packages/platform/src/version-questions.ts`. `celldPreparedNoHostRegister` gains `platform:register@28`, and `celldSmokeOwnedPlanRegister` gains the same pin. Both keep their old pins, so a retained unpublished or repository-binding plan still prepares and still counts as the smoke's own plan. The seal row is e13a31cf…, and the family-answer test lists both questions under Register 28.\n- `scripts/celld-smoke.mjs`. The plan phase now uses the CLI's base default. `celldReference` checks a reference with `isScopeRef`, which requires exactly `scope` and `genesis`, and reports those two fields. The old `ref` check required `kind` and `inc`, which the current reference shape does not have. The invitation and the joined store now must match the room's membership on both scope and genesis, where the old check compared the scope only. `celldSmokeOperation` lets only 27 named stage names cross into the proxy's error line, and `scripts/test-celld-proxy.mjs` adds that one field.\n- LC-3. The room row in `wrangler.lending.jsonc` and the sandbox `LENDING` mapping in `wrangler.rollout.jsonc` carry the same host object: screen origin `https://lending.inguz.space`, room origin `https://dap-lending.inguz.workers.dev`, directory `sc_5hagamav…`, item 2 and presentation 7217583c…. Those values match request 7b51d924 and install END 4b89c102. The presentation equals the one in `examples/lending/releases/0.3.0/application.dap.json`, the signed 0.3.0 packet, and not the open 0.4.0 value. `deploy-smoke.test.mjs` now expects both screen origins, and its two-way agreement case covers the room row and the mapping.\n- The measured identifiers. Only the `presentation` field of the open Lending 0.4.0 and Counter 0.4.0 changes, after `version-questions.ts` entered their bundles. Entry, definitions and semantic stay exact, and no file under a `releases/` directory changes, so neither signed packet moves. Rule 163de663 allows the change to an open version.\n- Both notes, and the docs changes in `docs/celld.md`, `docs/hosts.md`, `docs/self-host-mac.md` and `docs/testing.md`.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 2055762c is an ancestor. The 25 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 2055762c e18b6c71`. From 5fd226c6 to the head only the two notes change. From the gated source 25f070a7 to 5fd226c6 only the two identifier files and `docs/testing.md` change.\n- The original gate, END a18e2cec: FAIL, and it stays FAIL. `gate.log` has SHA-256 2e6bfdb8… and `result.json` has 3f11a1cc…. The log names head 25f070a7 and tree b2e9fb98 with 0 changed files. Its one failure is the release reproduction case, and its last line is \"gate FAILED\".\n- The follow-up under rulings 7e4bf8ba and 42140027, END 2005b6dd: PASS at 5fd226c6. `result.json` in `2026-11-15-cb1-ls1-lc3-plain-native-followup-attempt1` names that head and tree with exit 0 and no first failure. The reproduction owner passed 1 of 1. The END reports Plain 4858 passed with 1 skipped and Native 1136 passed with 2 skipped. Node and Counting passed in the original gate on source that differs only by the two identifier fields and one guide sentence. Scale selected nothing, so no Scale case ran.\n- Page. END 718f2d46 records the four local macOS routes passing at 5fd226c6. No Linux Page or Card run is claimed.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 18 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. celld now prepares a base plan by default and still reads a retained plan of either old family. The content bucket and the trust setting enter a project only as one closed pair, and the JavaScript preparation and the Python deployment guard both use the production trust parser. The smoke reads the current reference shape through the shared `isScopeRef`. The Lending screen host has one value in the room and one mapping in the sandbox, and the existing test holds them equal.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding.\n\n- The pair is closed. A bucket without trust, trust without a bucket, a second bucket, another binding or bucket name, or an extra key in the row refuses in both preparation and deployment. Trust text that the production parser refuses also refuses. The text stays public and nonsecret, and only that text crosses to the child process.\n- Validation comes early. Preparation checks the trust file before it creates the output directory. Deployment runs every closed file, mode and configuration check before it starts the child.\n- Error output stays safe. Each refusal prints a fixed message, and the proxy reports a stage name only when it is one of the 27 maintained names.\n- Authority does not change. No lease, custody, session or grant code changes. The two new register pins only admit Base plans to the existing celld questions.\n- The smoke's identity check is stronger. The invitation and the join must name the room's exact membership history, scope and genesis.\n- LC-3 maps one screen host to the installed 0.3.0 presentation. A member reaches only the screen of the active install item 2.\n\nOne fact for the record: `check_application_trust` finds `node` on `PATH`. The operator's environment already chooses the Node that runs preparation, so this adds no new trust in the environment. The guard refuses when `node` is missing.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The Python guard repeats the one-row bucket shape because Python cannot import the module. It sends trust grammar to the one production parser instead of copying it.\n\nQualifications that stand: the original full gate is FAIL, and the follow-up is a ruled partial run. The Page routes ran on macOS only. The recorded POST playback checks no fresh signature, and claim founding uses simulated transport loss. No Linux CI, hosted install, provider, fleet, Card or NF-7 result follows. Ruling 841b7903 keeps the fleet witness separate, and CB-2 owns the archive provider. LS-1 closes at the joint landing under 3f739d53. This approval authorizes no push, landing, deployment or signing. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:81194b0fc5dbadee6a786f1f5bd7b9b1dc46742b","binding":"assigned","head":"e18b6c71655fa477594a507129eb69bafbda8390","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:939fa1988eb0d6166f398e3523162c169412c18d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9b08303214a9f1381cfb7e47e0af6ea3be265a6d\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:630a37a06c656fc848ec4d270bbbb0eb13f5a151\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fa55582bec9dade2d64ef1226b45101781d4194f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:939fa1988eb0d6166f398e3523162c169412c18d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}